From c2e37e20e9ab473c062e0f88272d1902bfb7cdf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benbrastmckie <benbrastmckie@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:43:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Logics/Modal): make modal Proposition fully primitive
 {atom,bot,imp,and,or,box,diamond}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reshapes the modal Proposition inductive type from the diamond-primitive
{atom, not, and, diamond} basis to the fully-primitive
{atom, bot, imp, and, or, box, diamond} basis, with `not` derived as
`imp · .bot` (and `or`/`box` correspondingly derivable/primitive per the
new basis). This trades a smaller primitive set for full connective
primitivity matching standard modal logic presentations, at the cost of
`not` and `and` becoming derived forms whose denotation must be proved
rather than assumed definitionally.

Builds green against #607's existing minimal K/T cube (Cube.lean
unchanged), demonstrating the reshape is backward compatible with the
current cube-completion approach in this PR.

Adds one grind_lint skip line for `Cslib.Logic.Modal.not_denotation` in
CslibTests/GrindLint.lean: its proof now routes through the derived-negation
`grind =` lemma set (negation is `imp · .bot` rather than a primitive
constructor), which triggers additional grind instantiations.

Co-authored-by: Claude Code (Anthropic) <noreply@anthropic.com>
